===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|zeitgeister|zeitgeisten}}

# The [[spirit]] of the [[age]]; the [[taste]], [[outlook]], and [[spirit]] [[characteristic]] of a [[period]].
#: {{syn|en|spiritus mundi|temper of the times|tenor of the times}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1958|title={{w|Stride Toward Freedom}}|chapter=Rosa Parks' Arrest|author=Martin Luther King Jr.|authorlink=Martin Luther King Jr.|passage=She was anchored to that seat by the accumulated indignities of days gone by and the boundless aspirations of generations yet unborn. She was a victim of both the forces of history and the forces of destiny. She had been tracked down by the '''Zeitgeist'''—the spirit of the time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=Michael Vanden Heuvel|title=Elmer Rice: A Research and Production Sourcebook|publisher=Greenwood Publishing Group|ISBN=9780313274312|passage=After quickly summarizing the '''zeitgeisten''' of the Greek, Elizabethan, and early modern periods and their effects on the theatre, Rice turns to the contemporary world.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2007-dec-09-ca-heinlein9-story.html|title=The descent of a sci-fi guru|date=2007-12-09|author=Scott Timberg|quotee=Annalee Newitz|work=Los Angeles Times|passage=[Robert] Heinlein’s gift was to catch the '''zeitgeist'''. “That’s what made him so successful, but it makes his work seem dated.”}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2014-02-10|author=Anthony Faiola|title=Swiss vote to limit foreign workers captures growing European fears about immigration
|work=The Washington Post|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140211042515/http://www.washingtonpost.com/world/europe/swiss-vote-to-limit-foreign-workers-captures-growing-european-fears-about-immigration/2014/02/10/e0dfd354-9254-11e3-b3f7-f5107432ca45_story.html|archivedate=2014-02-11|url=http://www.washingtonpost.com/world/europe/swiss-vote-to-limit-foreign-workers-captures-growing-european-fears-about-immigration/2014/02/10/e0dfd354-9254-11e3-b3f7-f5107432ca45_story.html|passage=The vote also stoked fears that Swiss citizens were reflecting the '''zeitgeist''' across Europe, where right-wing populists increasingly are seizing the spotlight with an anti-immigration political agenda.}}

====Usage notes====
* The German term, {{m|de|Zeitgeist}}, is commonly not pluralized. {{m|de|Geist||ghost, spirit}} however has the plural ''Geister''.

